# GitHub issue / PR workflow

For every discrete feature or fix in this repo:

1. Implement and smoke-test (API and/or build) before opening GitHub items.
2. Create an **English** GitHub issue and PR; link with `Closes #N`.
3. Apply labels (`crm`, `ui`, `website`, `mobile`, `api`, `infra`, `enhancement` as fits).
4. Commit messages and PR/issue text must read like a normal developer wrote them — short, concrete, no AI filler, no mention of Cursor/Copilot/ChatGPT.
5. PR body: what changed, how you checked it, a short manual checklist. Skip generic “Summary / Test plan” fluff when a tighter note is clearer.
6. Prefer stacking PRs on the current feature tip when the change depends on unmerged work; otherwise open against `main`.
